Actually I already have some simple hierarchical model which gives slightly better results than poisson pseudo maximum likelihood but I wonder if it is possible to make the model more "hierarchical" to capture variability even better.
transformed parameters {
    for (i in 1:N) {
        eta[i] <- ...;
        log_lik[i] <- neg_binomial_2_log_log(Y[i], eta[i], phi[i]);
    }
}
model {
    phi ~ lognormal(0, sigma_phi);
    sigma_phi ~ cauchy(0, 2);
}
Thank you,
Linas

