Did you send the right .stan file?  The one attached didn't have
the constraint:

parameters...

	real CL[jend];
	real V1[jend];
	real V2[jend];

model ...

 	CL[j]~lognormal(logmuCL,tauCLinv);
    	V1[j]~lognormal(logmuV1,tauV1inv);
    	V2[j]~lognormal(logmuV2,tauV2inv);

You need to declare these as

  real<lower=0> CL[jend];

This will stop these messages:

> stan::prob::lognormal_log(N4stan5agrad3varE): Random variable is -0.183312:0, but must be >= 0!

which are telling you that the left-hand-side variable
for the lognormal sampling statement is negative.

