On Friday, April 10, 2015 at 4:37:35 PM UTC-4, Andrew Gelman wrote:
> I don’t like this:  (crossprod(matrix) - N * tcrossprod(mean_vector)) / (N - 1);
> because it violates the principle of subtracting the mean before doing the crossproduct.

I've never heard of that principle. They are equivalent symbolically. That line might be more numerically unstable with a huge matrix and widely varying columns. But it is one line (if you already have the mean vector), preserves symmetry, and minimizes the autodiffing.

Ben

