That's a really big model and I'm not sure I can debug it by eye. I'd suggest commenting out half your model and continuing to do that until you find out which assignment is mismatched. The error message is telling you that you're trying to assign a matrix to a vector. (I got that from "found R1=-1; C1=1; R2=-1; C2=-1" -- the left side is R1, C1, the right side is R2, C2; -1 is Eigen's way of representing a dynamic size.)

