I'm looking to explore using stan for real-time bayesian estimation of gaze position during eye tracking. As the data streams in, I'll need to use the posterior from analysis of y[i-1] as the prior for datum y[i]. Is there a way to directly provide samples as priors rather than the more typical specification of distributions?

